OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786506479
OL,3,CParts of country may hit 38C as fire
OL,4,Cunion chief warns of 'national
OL,5,Cemergency'
OL,7,FMet Office chief forecaster Chris
OL,8,FBulmer said: "While the peak heat will
OL,9,Fbe more short-lived than recent
OL,10,Fheatwaves, temperatures widely into
OL,11,Fthe mid-30s Celsius on Thursday brings
OL,12,Fthe potential for impacts for some,
OL,13,Fwhich is why a Met Office warning has
OL,14,Fbeen issued.
OL,26,@pD@NOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30504
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786506479
OL,3,CParts of country may hit 38C as fire
OL,4,Cunion chief warns of 'national
OL,5,Cemergency'
OL,7,F"High pressure is now becoming
OL,8,Fdominant and temperatures will build
OL,9,Fday by day. Southerly and south-
OL,10,Feasterly winds will also tap into the
OL,11,Fhot conditions over Europe which helps
OL,12,Fdevelop this further notable heat in
OL,13,Fwhat has been a hot and dry summer so
OL,14,Ffar for many in the south of the UK."
OL,16,FSteve Wright, general secretary of the
OL,17,FFire Brigades Union, told Times Radio
OL,18,Fthat the country faces a national
OL,19,Femergency "right now", with blazes
OL,20,Fseen "all across" the UK.
OL,26,@oD@AOUvD@eO]{D@KOU{D@UO]|D@FOU|D@QO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/11
