OL,3,CParts of country may hit 38C as fire
OL,4,Cunion chief warns of 'national
OL,5,Cemergency'
OL,7,FNearly three quarters of England and
OL,8,Fthe whole of Wales are in drought,
OL,9,Fafter a record dry July and very dry
OL,10,Fstart to August has combined with high
OL,11,Ftemperatures to put pressure on water
OL,12,Fresources.
OL,14,FSouthern Water has applied for a rare
OL,15,Fdrought order which would ban
OL,16,Fbusinesses from non-essential water
OL,17,Fuse, including cleaning cars and
OL,18,Ffilling non-domestic swimming pools,
OL,19,Fsaying an "exceptional" lack of rain
OL,20,Fhas threatened supplies in Hampshire
OL,21,Fand the Isle of Wight.
OL,26,@{D@KOU{D@WO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30509
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786506479
OL,3,CParts of country may hit 38C as fire
OL,4,Cunion chief warns of 'national
OL,5,Cemergency'
OL,7,FIt warned that 165,000 people in the
OL,8,FSouthampton West supply area could
OL,9,Fface restricted supplies.
OL,11,FEnvironment Secretary Angela Eagle
OL,12,Fwill decide on the application, which
OL,13,Fwould be the first such ban since May
OL,14,F2006.
OL,16,FElsewhere, water stations opened in
OL,17,FIlford, east London, and Chigwell,
OL,18,FEssex, after burst water mains left
OL,19,Fhomes and businesses with no water or
OL,20,Flow water pressure since Sunday,
OL,21,FThames Water said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
